            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks good to me, but I'll defer to Matt on whether this should be on a separate interface.  Typical tradeoffs probably between making interfaces modular/specific vs. driving additional D-Bus calls that could impact performance."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This isn't going in the base Inventory.Item.  I'm not sure what the expectations are here but this \"collection status\" seems unique to IBM's openpower-vpd-* implementation."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "The expectation here is to know if the VPD associated with the FRU is valid and has been successfully collected. \nSince this interface populates properties reflecting attribute of a specific inventory, I thought of adding it here.\nJust like \"present\" which says if the Inventory item is present or not, this property can additionally state whether the VPD for the present FRU is valid or not.\nCurrently, it may look like IBM specific use case but in case not consumed will be defaulted to \"NotStarted\"?\n\nStill if it does not look like a fit here, then as @spinler@us.ibm.com suggested, I can move it to decorator interface as that is ok with all."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "For systems that use EM + fru-device, there isn't really a concept of 'VPD collection', not that EM even puts this iface on its objects though I believe some dbus-sensors apps do.\n\nMaybe it would be better to put this on an Inventory.Decorator interface?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
