        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "f2984f94f802516b030d3bf9076f58ad1f096a8a",
            "parents": [
                "1cc8bb4b4253ed5c3547bb9130c51a1a81736841"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/78/80478/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
            },
            "createdOn": 1749656115,
            "author": {
                "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
            },
            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "This whole concept is pretty much IBM specific, since by definition with the EM method 'VPD' has to be collected before there can even be an inventory object for it.\n\nSo maybe make a new decorator interface with just this property?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "And put it into com.ibm?  I don't have any visibility to how this is going to be used but I don't think we're expecting phosphor applications to use this, are we?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Well instead of IBM, I would say this concept is more PIM specific. PIM has the concept of persisting the data and pull that back to Dbus in case it restarts or BMC reboots and this property helps in establishing the validity of that data.\n\nMay not be applicable to EM specific implementations but then PIM is also part of phosphor application group."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Are you proposing something in PIM to update these values?  I know of no such proposal."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we consider using the [Progress.interface.yaml](https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Common/Progress.interface.yaml)?\n\nI believe the current description in the Progress interface is somewhat tailored to dumps or similar use cases. However, it seems like we could generalize the description to represent progress status for any type of operation, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "The progress interface talks about an additional delete interface that needs to be implemented, also it does have some extra properties which is not relevant with our use case as of now.\nHaving said that, we will still try to explore more and see if we are able to map it to our use case."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "If you can document what your use case is, maybe people can help point you in the right direction.  As of now, I do not know what the purpose of this is or how it would be used by any application (outside of maybe openpower-vpd-parser), so it's unlikely to be accepted into a xyz.openbmc_project interface as currently specified.  Maybe you need to write a design document?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "On a very high level, my idea behind proposing this property was to establish the validity of data hosted under PIM.\n\nPIM is used to host the data where as it does not collect that data itself. So always there will be another application which will collect the data and will use PIM to host that.\n\nNow, PIM has the feature of persisting the data hosted under it.\nSo, in case where BMC reboots, PIM will simply republish the data that it persisted in the previous boot, where as, there is be a possibility that some configuration changed between the reboots or the collection did not took place correctly in the next boot.\nGoing by the current design, there is no way to establish validity of data being published under PIM.\n\nThis property would help in establishing that.(I can rename the property to be more generic, if required.)\n\nAnyways, for now, I will try to see if the interface pointed to caters our use case, else will take this forward as suggested.\nThanks All."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This sounds like you'd actively need code changes in PIM in order to \"invalidate\" this value though?  That doesn't seem to be generally applicable.\n\nIs there a plan to get your systems moved to EM?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "> Is there a plan to get your systems moved to EM?\n\nNo, we have few use case constraints, not planning to move to EM any time soon."
                }
            ],
